{"id": "lotteries-waiting-lists-and-pools", "title": "Lotteries held up where they can be checked; pool work is shared far from evenly", "seconds": 140.1, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "c6ce7d259016f5b7", "words": 392, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "The question: in San Francisco’s lotteries,", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.33, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The same winners?", "sub": "lotteries, waiting lists and pools"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 1.32, 1.47, 1.69, 2.28]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "do the same people keep winning, over and over?", "t0": 3.33, "t1": 8.16, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The same winners?", "sub": "lotteries, waiting lists and pools"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.2, 0.34, 0.71, 1.05, 1.3, 2.31, 2.99, 3.25]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "We found 37 drawings, waiting lists and pools.", "t0": 8.16, "t1": 11.18, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The same winners?", "sub": "lotteries, waiting lists and pools"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.22, 0.5, 1.05, 1.67, 2.02, 2.35, 2.49]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[1]", "suspicious[3]"], "text": "To check, you need two lists: who entered, and who won.", "t0": 11.3, "t1": 14.54, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Who entered, and who won", "sub": "37 systems found"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.62, 0.76, 0.95, 1.22, 1.96, 2.18, 2.58, 2.75, 2.92]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[1]", "suspicious[3]"], "text": "How many of the 37 publish both?", "t0": 14.66, "t1": 17.03, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Who entered, and who won", "sub": "37 systems found"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.34, 0.41, 0.5, 1.01, 1.38]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "Just 7.", "t0": 17.03, "t1": 17.85, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "7", "label": "of 37 publish entrants and winners"}, "emph": ["Just"], "wt": [0.04, 0.32]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 18.37, "t1": 20.03, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.33, 0.4, 0.99, 1.17, 1.24]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "In 2018, the City Attorney returned 21 affordable homes to people who needed them.", "t0": 20.25, "t1": 24.8, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Official reviews", "sub": "19 passages, 5 on below-market housing"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.44, 1.26, 1.41, 1.66, 2.04, 2.42, 2.91, 3.32, 3.63, 3.74, 3.97, 4.09, 4.34]}, {"scene": "test", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "Only one drawing can be checked over many years.", "t0": 25.02, "t1": 27.18, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Condominium conversion lottery", "kicker": "The one real test", "sub": "2001 to 2013, 1,996 buildings"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.5, 0.81, 0.93, 1.03, 1.3, 1.48, 1.7]}, {"scene": "test", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "It’s the lottery to turn apartment buildings into condos,", "t0": 27.3, "t1": 30.01, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Condominium conversion lottery", "kicker": "The one real test", "sub": "2001 to 2013, 1,996 buildings"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.38, 0.82, 0.96, 1.16, 1.56, 1.94, 2.09]}, {"scene": "test", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "A building on its first try won 3.3 percent of the time. On its 8th try?", "t0": 30.13, "t1": 36.21, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["first entry", "3.3%"], "b": ["8th entry", "71.6%"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.5, 0.59, 0.74, 1.03, 1.39, 1.64, 2.01, 2.3, 2.59, 3.03, 3.14, 3.23, 4.34, 4.52, 4.71, 5.02]}, {"scene": "test", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "71.6 percent.", "t0": 36.21, "t1": 38.18, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "71.6%", "label": "win rate on the 8th entry"}, "emph": ["71.6"], "wt": [0.04, 0.88, 1.21, 1.51]}, {"scene": "test", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[2]", "established[3]"], "text": "A losing building gets an extra ticket for every lottery it lost, with no cap.", "t0": 38.7, "t1": 42.75, "shot": "b8r", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "one extra ticket for every lottery it lost, with no cap", "kicker": "Subdivision Code section 1396.3"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.47, 0.78, 0.96, 1.04, 1.31, 1.6, 1.77, 2.02, 2.35, 2.45, 3.31, 3.5, 3.67]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "The first lead is work pools. A department picks several firms, then hands out jobs as needed.", "t0": 42.97, "t1": 48.65, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Work pools", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "64 pools of firms"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.44, 0.74, 0.9, 1.14, 2.09, 2.21, 2.63, 2.92, 3.29, 4.15, 4.34, 4.59, 4.77, 5.19, 5.33]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "In 17 of 64 pools, one firm took half or more.", "t0": 48.77, "t1": 52.44, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Work pools", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "64 pools of firms"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.8, 0.89, 1.41, 2.22, 2.51, 2.81, 3.02, 3.25, 3.36]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[7]"], "text": "The contract Lee Incorporated leads took 81.3 percent", "t0": 52.56, "t1": 56.8, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Share of pool spending", "rows": [["Lee Incorporated’s contract", "81.3%"], ["Smith-Emery San Francisco", "69.8%"], ["an even share", "20%"]]}, "emph": ["81.3 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.7, 0.95, 1.56, 2.16, 2.45, 3.0, 3.32, 3.59]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[7]"], "text": "of a 7.1 million dollar water department pool.", "t0": 56.8, "t1": 59.6, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Share of pool spending", "rows": [["Lee Incorporated’s contract", "81.3%"], ["Smith-Emery San Francisco", "69.8%"], ["an even share", "20%"]]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.21, 0.33, 0.69, 0.98, 1.23, 1.53, 1.79, 2.02, 2.43]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[7]"], "text": "Part went on to subcontractors. Lee Incorporated’s own payments are 50.3 percent of the pool.", "t0": 59.72, "t1": 65.25, "shot": "b18x", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["the contract Lee Incorporated leads", "81.3%"], "b": ["Lee Incorporated’s own payments", "50.3%"]}, "emph": ["50.3 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.45, 0.58, 0.66, 2.11, 2.32, 3.02, 3.23, 3.61, 3.79, 4.16, 4.43, 4.69, 5.01, 5.06, 5.16]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "The second lead is one group behind many wins.", "t0": 65.47, "t1": 68.2, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "San Francisco Parks Alliance", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "fiscal sponsor of 11 of 19 awards"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.52, 0.78, 0.98, 1.22, 1.52, 1.89, 2.2]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "In 2022, one sponsor stood behind 11 of 19 awards.", "t0": 68.32, "t1": 72.27, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "San Francisco Parks Alliance", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "fiscal sponsor of 11 of 19 awards"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.35, 1.15, 1.43, 1.91, 2.13, 2.4, 2.86, 3.03, 3.4]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "amount", "established[6]"], "text": "Fiscal 2021 to 2023: 2.3 million dollars.", "t0": 72.39, "t1": 76.99, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$2.3 million", "label": "in 27 awards with one fiscal sponsor", "sub": "San Francisco Parks Alliance"}, "emph": ["2.3 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.41, 0.74, 1.25, 1.35, 1.65, 2.85, 3.13, 3.4, 3.72, 4.08]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "amount", "established[6]"], "text": "None on the 2026 list.", "t0": 77.51, "t1": 79.14, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$2.3 million", "label": "in 27 awards with one fiscal sponsor", "sub": "San Francisco Parks Alliance"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.32, 0.4, 0.68, 1.26]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "The third lead is scored rounds, where the best score should win.", "t0": 79.76, "t1": 82.84, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["first 4 rounds", "1 of 21 funded"], "b": ["since", "32 of 43 funded"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.43, 0.64, 0.75, 1.11, 1.75, 1.92, 2.01, 2.24, 2.55, 2.76]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "Twice, a lower-scored project beat a higher one.", "t0": 82.96, "t1": 85.9, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "a lower-scored San Francisco one in the same pool won"}, "wt": [0.0, 1.02, 1.15, 1.72, 2.13, 2.31, 2.38, 2.67]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[4]"], "text": "That’s because both were bond rounds, left to another State committee’s scoring. Its rules aren’t on file.", "t0": 86.02, "t1": 92.15, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "a lower-scored San Francisco one in the same pool won"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.51, 0.79, 0.94, 1.19, 1.95, 2.22, 2.34, 2.64, 2.88, 3.26, 4.3, 4.61, 5.26, 5.58, 5.77]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "In the 9 percent rounds, 9 of 11 San Francisco applications were funded. None was passed over.", "t0": 92.27, "t1": 98.57, "shot": "b16n", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "The 9% rounds", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "9 of 11 San Francisco applications funded", "chip": "none passed over"}, "emph": ["None was passed over"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.23, 0.52, 0.9, 1.73, 2.09, 2.19, 2.52, 2.73, 3.22, 3.84, 4.0, 5.01, 5.44, 5.65, 5.98]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "25 of the 37 systems can’t be tested at all.", "t0": 98.79, "t1": 102.12, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Cannot be checked", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "25 of 37 systems"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.75, 0.85, 0.94, 1.5, 2.27, 2.5, 2.61, 2.95, 3.05]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "The fifth lead is housing lotteries.", "t0": 102.34, "t1": 103.84, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Affordable housing lotteries", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "74 listings, 689 homes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.38, 0.58, 0.69, 1.02]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "74 listings offered 689 homes.", "t0": 103.96, "t1": 108.77, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Affordable housing lotteries", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "74 listings, 689 homes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.68, 1.24, 1.59, 1.92, 2.42, 3.28]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "How many applications came in?", "t0": 108.77, "t1": 111.21, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Affordable housing lotteries", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "74 listings, 689 homes"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.21, 0.4, 1.03, 1.27]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "128,010.", "t0": 111.21, "t1": 113.5, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "128,010", "label": "applications for 689 homes"}, "emph": ["128,010"], "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.6, 1.09, 1.72]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why"], "text": "Some applicants get first pick, like people who live or work here.", "t0": 114.02, "t1": 117.16, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "applicants holding a preference alone outnumbered the homes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.73, 0.95, 1.29, 1.83, 2.01, 2.23, 2.38, 2.54, 2.66, 2.89]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why"], "text": "In all 74, those people alone outnumbered the homes.", "t0": 117.28, "t1": 120.94, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "applicants holding a preference alone outnumbered the homes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.4, 1.54, 1.9, 2.19, 2.6, 3.07, 3.18]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why"], "text": "So without that, you couldn’t win, however the drawing fell.", "t0": 121.06, "t1": 124.14, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "applicants holding a preference alone outnumbered the homes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.49, 0.94, 1.08, 1.37, 1.93, 2.28, 2.37, 2.73]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Nothing here shows a drawing was rigged.", "t0": 124.36, "t1": 126.08, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any drawing was rigged", "Who applied and lost"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.45, 0.76, 0.84, 1.19, 1.35]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Where both lists exist, the same names don’t win against the odds.", "t0": 126.2, "t1": 130.04, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any drawing was rigged", "Who applied and lost"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.55, 0.97, 1.8, 1.96, 2.29, 2.65, 2.85, 2.98, 3.25, 3.39]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "Applicant lists for every program, and the logs showing who got each job in the pools.", "t0": 130.16, "t1": 134.61, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Applicant lists for winners-only programs"}, {"who": "", "what": "The work-order logs for each pool"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.43, 0.67, 0.85, 1.16, 1.85, 2.01, 2.11, 2.45, 2.77, 2.95, 3.19, 3.45, 3.77, 3.87, 3.94]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "No authority has ruled on any of these drawings.", "t0": 134.73, "t1": 137.03, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.64, 0.78, 1.11, 1.3, 1.53, 1.62, 1.79]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 137.15, "t1": 139.25, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.31, 0.4, 0.47, 1.18, 1.36, 1.45]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "On the record", "test": "The one real test", "lead1": "Lead 1 · one firm takes most", "lead2": "Lead 2 · one sponsor", "lead3": "Lead 3 · scored rounds", "lead4": "Lead 4 · can’t be checked", "lead5": "Lead 5 · 128,010 applications", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "map", "hook": "question"}